:**\n\n- In **Frame 12**, a **moose** is visible in the distance, standing among the snow-covered shrubs.\n- The man’s gloved hand is pointing towards the moose, indicating they have spotted it.\n- However, **there is no evidence that they shoot at or attempt to hunt the moose**.\n- The rifle is not aimed at the moose, and no shooting action is depicted. The man and boy appear to be observing it from a distance.\n- The moose is not approached, and the subsequent frames show the family continuing their journey without any further interaction with the moose.\n- Therefore, the moose is **avoided** as a target; it is merely observed as part of the wildlife in the environment.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe man and boy are engaged in a winter bird-hunting expedition in Alaska. They use a single rifle, which is carried by both of them at different times. They successfully hunt and harvest at least one white ptarmigan, which is displayed and stored in their snowmobile. They also encounter a moose in the distance but do not attempt to hunt it, choosing instead to observe it. The overall activity is focused on small-game hunting, with the boy actively participating and the man guiding and documenting the experience.\n", '\n=== Batch 30-31 (1 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1575.jpg\nVLM Response: In the provided frame (Frame 1575), **no family members are visible** — neither the man in the camouflage/black jacket nor the boy in the blue coat appear in this shot. The image is a **close-up, tightly framed view of a snowmobile’s handlebar and dashboard area**. Visible components include:\n\n- A black handlebar grip and control panel.\n- A mounted electronic device (possibly a GPS or communication unit) with buttons.\n- A shock absorber or suspension component labeled “FOX,” indicating high-performance snowmobile equipment.\n- A circular emblem or sticker with a logo (possibly a brand or race insignia) near the right side of th